  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/TB - Namibia (01-Jan-2018-31-Dec-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namibia, TB/HIV, Namibia Network of AIDS Service Organizations (NANASO)This program has the following goals: To reduce new HIV infections and AIDS related mortality by 75% by 2022 from 2015 levels, and move towards ending AIDS as a public health threat by 2030.  To reduce the national burden of TB by achieving fewer than ten TB patients per 100,000 population by 2019. The objectives of this program are: To reduce new HIV infections by 75% by 2020.  To reduce HIV related deaths by 75% by 2020.  To enroll and retain 100% of newly identified PLHIV on ART by 2020.  To reduce TB/HIV co-infection rates.  To accelerate the appropriate detection and diagnosis of TB.  To manage all forms of TB, among all ages and including drug-resistant and drug-sensitive TB, including complications</narrative>
  </description>
